{
    "$schema": "https://docs.sentry.io/api/alerts/issue-alert-rule/",
    "comment": "Source of truth for the 10 Sentry alert rules in arkova-worker (SCRUM-1254 / R0-8 + SCRUM-1308 / R0-8-FU2 + SCRUM-1247 / R0-1). Sentry MCP cannot create issue alert rules; an admin opens https://arkova.sentry.io/alerts/rules/ and creates each rule below 1:1. Update this file alongside any UI change. SCRUM-1062 (BQ export pipeline) added 2 rules: consecutive-failure on incremental cron and any-failure on daily snapshot. SCRUM-1805 (PR #753) added 1 rule: any-failure on webhook delivery_log insert (first-occurrence page; steady state is zero events). SCRUM-3050 added 2 rules for the pipeline-throughput dead-man: a baseline route and a level>=fatal SUSTAINED escalation route. NOTE: the rule count in this comment has drifted before — count the `rules` array, do not trust a number in prose. NOTE 2: a rule in this file is a DECLARATION, not a working alarm. Nothing here is live until an admin creates it in the Sentry UI and a live delivery (a real Slack message) is captured. ENVIRONMENT SCOPE (2026-08-17): every rule now carries \"environment\": \"production\" — set it in the Environment dropdown at the top of the Sentry rule editor when creating or updating a rule. Previously no rule had one, which was harmless only because the soak rigs have no SENTRY_DSN; the moment a rig gets one (a Cloud Run env change, no code review) every unscoped rule would route rig events to #ops identically to prod. resolveSentryEnvironment (services/worker/src/utils/sentry.ts) already guarantees that only K_SERVICE=arkova-worker earns the 'production' tag — rigs run NODE_ENV=production and tag themselves with their own service name — so the scope is exact. The one emitter that does NOT go through Sentry.init is .github/workflows/revision-drift.yml, which POSTs a hand-built envelope; it now stamps environment itself or the SCRUM-1247 rule would stop matching. Parity is enforced by scripts/ci/check-sentry-alert-environment-scope.test.ts.",
    "project": "arkova-worker",
    "rules": [
        {
            "name": "SCRUM-1254 — pg_cron job failures",
            "environment": "production",
            "actionMatch": "all",
            "filterMatch": "all",
            "conditions": [
                {
                    "id": "sentry.rules.conditions.event_frequency.EventFrequencyCondition",
                    "value": 3,
                    "interval": "20m"
                }
            ],
            "filters": [
                {
                    "id": "sentry.rules.filters.tagged_event.TaggedEventFilter",
                    "key": "source",
                    "match": "eq",
                    "value": "db-health-monitor"
                },
                {
                    "id": "sentry.rules.filters.tagged_event.TaggedEventFilter",
                    "key": "alert_type",
                    "match": "eq",
                    "value": "pg_cron_failure"
                }
            ],
            "actions": [
                {
                    "id": "sentry.integrations.slack.notify_action.SlackNotifyServiceAction",
                    "channel": "#ops",
                    "tags": "story,jobid"
                }
            ],
            "frequency": 60
        },
        {
            "name": "SCRUM-1254 — Dead-tuple ratio > threshold for > 1h",
            "environment": "production",
            "actionMatch": "all",
            "filterMatch": "all",
            "conditions": [
                {
                    "id": "sentry.rules.conditions.event_frequency.EventFrequencyCondition",
                    "value": 12,
                    "interval": "1h"
                }
            ],
            "filters": [
                {
                    "id": "sentry.rules.filters.tagged_event.TaggedEventFilter",
                    "key": "source",
                    "match": "eq",
                    "value": "db-health-monitor"
                },
                {
                    "id": "sentry.rules.filters.tagged_event.TaggedEventFilter",
                    "key": "alert_type",
                    "match": "eq",
                    "value": "dead_tuple_ratio"
