                }
            ],
            "frequency": 60
        },
        {
            "name": "SCRUM-1805 — Webhook delivery_log insert failure",
            "comment": "PR #753 dispatcher fix wrapped the delivery_log insert path with Sentry.captureException after the pre-existing PG 22P02 UUID-coercion bug ran undetected for the lifetime of PR #734. Any non-zero rate of `subsystem:webhooks AND stage:delivery_log_insert` indicates the dispatcher cannot persist a delivery row — customer events are being silently dropped at the storage layer (pre-fix this was a UUID type mismatch; post-fix it would be a DB outage, RLS regression, or schema drift). Threshold = 1 occurrence / 5 minutes; we want a page on first occurrence rather than a frequency-based pattern because the steady-state expectation is zero.",
            "environment": "production",
            "actionMatch": "all",
            "filterMatch": "all",
            "conditions": [
                {
                    "id": "sentry.rules.conditions.event_frequency.EventFrequencyCondition",
                    "value": 1,
                    "interval": "5m"
                }
            ],
            "filters": [
                {
                    "id": "sentry.rules.filters.tagged_event.TaggedEventFilter",
                    "key": "subsystem",
                    "match": "eq",
                    "value": "webhooks"
                },
                {
                    "id": "sentry.rules.filters.tagged_event.TaggedEventFilter",
                    "key": "stage",
                    "match": "eq",
                    "value": "delivery_log_insert"
                }
            ],
            "actions": [
                {
                    "id": "sentry.integrations.slack.notify_action.SlackNotifyServiceAction",
                    "channel": "#ops",
                    "tags": "event_type,endpoint_id,subsystem"
                }
            ],
            "frequency": 60
        },
        {
            "name": "SCRUM-2902 — Credential Engine API key expiry",
            "comment": "Fail-LOUD expiry alarm for the CE partnership API key / CTID publishing credential (R-1 FATAL launch dependency). services/worker/src/jobs/ce-key-expiry-alert.ts emits a Sentry event at T-30/T-14/T-7 and continuously after expiry, and fires EVERY daily run with expiry_window=SENTINEL when CE_API_KEY_EXPIRES_AT is unset/placeholder. This rule is what turns those events into a human page (Slack #ops) — event ≠ alert. FirstSeenEventCondition pages on each new day's issue (the message carries the changing day count) so the countdown is a daily reminder while in-window. Tag/channel parity enforced by scripts/ci/check-ce-key-expiry-alert-contract.test.ts. An admin must create this rule 1:1 at https://arkova.sentry.io/alerts/rules/ (Sentry MCP cannot create issue alert rules) AND a live delivery test (real Slack page) must be captured per the SCRUM-2902 runbook before this is considered wired.",
            "environment": "production",
            "actionMatch": "all",
            "filterMatch": "all",
            "conditions": [
                {
                    "id": "sentry.rules.conditions.first_seen_event.FirstSeenEventCondition"
                }
            ],
            "filters": [
                {
                    "id": "sentry.rules.filters.tagged_event.TaggedEventFilter",
                    "key": "source",
                    "match": "eq",
                    "value": "ce-key-expiry"
                },
                {
                    "id": "sentry.rules.filters.level.LevelFilter",
                    "match": "gte",
                    "level": "30"
                }
            ],
            "actions": [
                {
                    "id": "sentry.integrations.slack.notify_action.SlackNotifyServiceAction",
                    "channel": "#ops",
                    "tags": "story,expiry_window,days_until_expiry"
                }
            ],
            "frequency": 720
        },
        {
            "name": "SCRUM-3050 — Pipeline throughput dead-man",
            "comment": "The pipeline-throughput dead-man (services/worker/src/jobs/pipelineThroughputMonitor.ts) CORRECTLY detected the 70h anchoring outage and fired every ~30 min for 70+ hours with an accurate diagnosis — and no human ever saw it, because there was no alert rule routing its events anywhere. Two defects were fixed together: (1) the capture helper carried source/story in `extra` only, so no TaggedEventFilter could ever have matched it — it now emits real TAGS; (2) one stable fingerprint meant every re-fire folded into a single aged issue. This rule is the baseline route to a human for any firing of the monitor. Tag parity is enforced by scripts/ci/check-pipeline-throughput-alert-contract.test.ts. An admin must create this rule 1:1 at https://arkova.sentry.io/alerts/rules/ (Sentry MCP cannot create issue alert rules) AND capture a live Slack delivery before it counts as wired.",
            "environment": "production",
            "actionMatch": "all",
            "filterMatch": "all",
            "conditions": [
                {
                    "id": "sentry.rules.conditions.first_seen_event.FirstSeenEventCondition"
                }
            ],
            "filters": [
                {
                    "id": "sentry.rules.filters.tagged_event.TaggedEventFilter",
                    "key": "source",
                    "match": "eq",
                    "value": "pipeline-throughput-monitor"
                },
                {
                    "id": "sentry.rules.filters.level.LevelFilter",
                    "match": "gte",
                    "level": "40"
                }
            ],
            "actions": [
                {
                    "id": "sentry.integrations.slack.notify_action.SlackNotifyServiceAction",
                    "channel": "#ops",
                    "tags": "story,sustained_bucket,alert_type"
                }
            ],
            "frequency": 60
        },
        {
            "name": "SCRUM-3050 — Pipeline throughput dead-man SUSTAINED (72h+)",
            "comment": "Escalation route. The monitor stamps a duration bucket (t24h/t48h/t72h/t168h) into its Sentry fingerprint, so crossing a boundary opens a genuinely NEW issue and re-triggers FirstSeenEventCondition instead of silently incrementing a stale one; past 72h the level escalates to fatal. This rule keys on level>=fatal (50) so a sustained outage pages on a separate, louder route than the routine error stream, with a 30-minute frequency rather than 60. This is the rule that would have re-paged during hours 24, 48 and 72 of the 2026-07-29 -> 2026-08-01 anchoring outage.",
            "environment": "production",
            "actionMatch": "all",
            "filterMatch": "all",
            "conditions": [
                {
                    "id": "sentry.rules.conditions.first_seen_event.FirstSeenEventCondition"
                }
            ],
            "filters": [
                {
                    "id": "sentry.rules.filters.tagged_event.TaggedEventFilter",
                    "key": "source",
                    "match": "eq",
                    "value": "pipeline-throughput-monitor"
                },
                {
                    "id": "sentry.rules.filters.level.LevelFilter",
                    "match": "gte",
                    "level": "50"
                }
            ],
            "actions": [
                {
                    "id": "sentry.integrations.slack.notify_action.SlackNotifyServiceAction",
                    "channel": "#ops",
                    "tags": "story,sustained_bucket,alert_type"
                }
            ],
            "frequency": 30
        }
    ],
